body:
This issue is closed, but I could reproduce the errors when trying to generate multiple scripts simultaneously from an EditorPlugin, each finishing with: 
```
ResourceSaver.Save(myScript, myPath);
EditorInterface.Singleton.GetResourceFilesystem().Scan();
```

If someone encounters a similar issue, and finds this thread, the easier fix is generating and saving all wanted scripts first, then calling `EditorInterface.Singleton.GetResourceFilesystem().Scan();` only once, after all resources are saved. 

Alternatively, a worse and funkier but functioning workaround is chaining deferred calls as such:
```
GenerateMyFirstScript(() =>
	Callable.From(() => GenerateMySecondScript(() =>
		Callable.From(() => GenerateMyThirdScript()).CallDeferred()
	)).CallDeferred()
);
```

Where each script invokes its successor if applicable:
```
private static void GenerateMyFirstScript(Action then = null)
{
	// . . . Generation code
	then?.Invoke();
}
```
